     "result_text_tail": "line:** approved as drafted.\n- **Reviewer changes:** I had a separate reviewer argue against the draft.\n  - It confirmed every number.\n  - The no-migration case is now the base case, and the move to D is shown only as the best case.\n  - Payback is quoted from the start of the project.\n  - The renewals must keep 2029 exit rights.\n  - The $350K of cash left after the redesign has to cover requalification and bundle-fill fixes that nobody has costed yet.\n- **Engineering time on D:** the pack gives no figure for what four months of engineering time on D is worth, so the deck lists it as an open question instead of estimating it.\n- **Money format:** the renderer rounds millions to one decimal, so figures like $0.55M would have shown as $0.6M. I show those in thousands instead ($550K, $750K, $1,250K).\n\n**Sourcing:** all 63 numbers come from the briefing pack: 33 taken directly and 30 calculated, which appear as live formulas in the workbook. Three are estimates, each shown with its basis on the slide. There are no placeholders and nothing was taken from the web. The final check passes with one warning, which I kept on purpose: the $750K best case isn't calculated from the slide's chart.\n\nYou could switch the theme, or add a backup slide modelling a sunset at a different date once the 2027\u201328 test results are in.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `vesper-connector-c.pptx`\n- `vesper-connector-c-sources.xlsx`\n- `vesper-connector-c.json` (the spec; rebuild it with `work/build_spec.py`)"
